                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_435">Oxford, Oxfordshire. Merton
                        College. </orgName><p>‘Perhaps originally a Franciscan book. At the head of
                        f. viv is ‘Istum librum reparauerunt Magister Willelmus Emyldon M. Ricardus
                        Langstone M. Thomas Bloxham M. Ricardus Scarburgh Magister Iohannes Yonge’.
                        Emyldon was fellow 1441–52, Langstone c. 1446–52 (when he died), Bloxham c.
                        1449–61, Scarborough c. 1449, still in 1464, Yonge c. 1449–61 (BRUO 642,
                        1098, 204–5, 1651–2, 2135).’ (Thomson, Merton, 50)</p></provenance>
